2026-10-04T09:00Z MinhHaDuong note AUTHOR AMENDMENT — HONEST BLOCKED IS NOT A DNF ("si le refus est la bonne réponse c'est lui qui vaut 10 et pas zéro"). Evidence that motivated it: ticket 0470's reference PR (e1e959d9) contains NO code — it requalifies the ticket needs-human and documents; the ticket body itself says "This is the one step of 0365 an agent cannot perform". The correct answer on 0470 is the documented refusal, yet the rubric's DNF=0 rule scored the honest refusers (C, E) zero while partial workers (D 18, F 24) were credited. Rubric amended (judge-rubric.md): an honest impossibility verdict is judged normally from 10 — deductions for doable work skipped, wrong impossibility claims, or vague owner instructions; DNF reserved for missing/dead submissions only. Re-judgement of all four recorded 0470 legs (c, d, e, f) under the amended rubric launched; old verdicts preserved in judges-dnf-v1/. The amendment is prospective-consistent: the voided re-runs (0470-b) and 0470-a will be judged under the amended rubric directly. Principle recorded: the boxing frame measures the answer, and when the right answer is "this is the owner's move", refusing well IS doing the work. AUTHOR REFINEMENT (v2, 2026-10-04): the clause covers FACTUAL impossibility only — browser/owner-only actions. A principled or ideological refusal (declining work the model could in fact perform: safety objections, "this is a human decision", role objections) is NOT covered: judged as work not done under normal tariffs (REROLL if the refusal invalidates the task). A needs-human LABEL is evidence to weigh, not a license. Rubric updated with a SCOPE OF THE CLAUSE block. PACKAGING BUG found mid-re-judge: judge.py excluded RESULT.md from the diff by design, so a pure-BLOCKED submission (empty diff) reached judges as a completely empty package — the honest refusals of 0470-c/e were invisible, which is why they scored DNF-zero even under the amended rubric (D 18 / F 24 had non-empty diffs, hence their points). Fixed: when the submission diff is empty, judge.py now attaches the branch's RESULT.md as a VERDICT DOCUMENT (producer names scrubbed). Re-judge rounds: judges-dnf-v1/ preserves the original zeros; the first amended round ran before the packaging fix and is superseded; final round (patched package + v2 rubric) re-judges 0470-c/d/e/f on gemini+kimi — the DeepSeek seat is DRY (HTTP 402, balance -0.00; author top-up needed), its missing verdicts to be redone after top-up.
