2026-10-05T13:30Z MinhHaDuong note STRATA DUAL-GPU INVESTIGATION (author ask: investigate/explain/strategize, incl. PRs and Issues — repo Niko1221/Strata). STATE ON PADME (from the B2 smoke logs): layer split auto gives K=47/48 to the A4000 (48 SMs, 0.97 ms/layer); the RTX 3060 (28 SMs, 1.46 ms/layer) hosts ONE layer + LM head + MTP (835 MiB) + the expert cache (4509 slots, 8.54 GiB) — the author's observed 88%/20% GPU load is BY DESIGN under the pipeline split: GPU0 is the pipeline, GPU1 is an expert-cache tier. The dev's own bench (2026-09-29, 5080+3090) settles the intuitions: auto beats manual K=30 (97 vs 85 tok/s), helper cards are SLOWER, and the second GPU's value is its VRAM as expert cache (hits 59-71% single → 96-97% dual, which is where the +14-31% decode comes from). B2's cold-cache 69.6% hit rate is the dormant lever: profile persistence (--expert-profile-save, capability MERGED as #477, present in our 0.1.38) is NOT enabled in our configs — every leg restarts cold and loads the generic 24,576-pair profile. CAVEAT #831 (open): the loaded profile's length CAPS the expert arena. UPSTREAM WAVE (all open, updated TODAY): the Hardin22/Strata-DualGPU cluster (#642 issue; #876 async adaptive tier, #905 pipelined windows + async tier "both cards working at the same time, 143 tok/s on RTX 5080 + 4060 Ti", #910 bounded attention merge + pipelined PLE read-ahead) — true dual-GPU parallel decode, the paradigm change; #936 stage hand-off overlap (STRATA_SPLIT_OVERLAP); issue #921 CPU-pool spin 20ms→100µs = +15% TG and 4x lower CPU on dual-4090 (padme's 50% CPU load is the symptom); #930 AVX2 decode rows (padme has no AVX-512 — direct fit); #733 CPU expert pipeline without phase barrier. KNOWN TRAPS: #690 native prefill kernels fail on the second GPU; #806 dual-5060Ti anomalies; #826 0.1.38→0.1.39 decode regression (HIP fix in flight) — stay on 0.1.38 for cycle 2. STRATEGY: freeze configs for cycle 2 (H2 speed comparability); in the 262K rerun enable per-model --expert-profile-save (fresh profiles, mind #831) and bench padme (auto vs profile-hot vs kv-resident sweep); track the Hardin22 cluster — if merged by cycle 3, run B2/B3 on the new build as a measured config version. Build version recorded as an experiment variable.
