2026-10-05T15:20Z MinhHaDuong note CPU UPGRADE ANALYSIS (author question: "est-ce que les cores Threadripper Pro 5945WX ont plus de SIMD ?"). Answer: NO — padme runs a TR PRO 3945WX (Zen 2, 12c, L3 64 MiB, AVX2-only, WRX80 8-channel DDR4 128 GB); the 5945WX is Zen 3 = SAME 256-bit AVX2, no AVX-512 (AMD's AVX-512 starts at Zen 4, sTR5 platform — not reachable by a CPU swap on this board). What the WRX80 platform does take drop-in: the TR Pro 5000 line — 5955X 16c / 5975WX 32c / 5995WX 64c; aggregate SIMD throughput scales with CORES (~2.7-5.3x at 32-64c), which is the real lever for Strata's CPU expert pool (the pool only serves cache MISSES). ORDER OF OPERATIONS RECORDED: (1) 5060 Ti first — +16 GB expert cache cuts misses, cutting CPU-pool work (same bottleneck from the other end); (2) then the --gpu-only-full bench to measure whether the CPU pool still floors the decode; (3) only then a CPU decision — cores (used Chagall), not SIMD, since no wider SIMD exists on this platform. AVX-512 would require a platform change (TR 7000 sTR5, or consumer Zen 5 which loses the 8-channel memory — a regression for the RAM-streaming expert pool).
2026-10-05T15:50Z MinhHaDuong note CPU UPGRADE OPTION VALIDATED: 3975WX Lenovo-locked <500 EUR (author found; padme IS a ThinkStation P620 — Lenovo-1046 board, so the "locked" chips pulled from P620s are by definition compatible: same socket, same 280W cooler, BIOS supports the line natively). Topology verified on the current 3945WX: 4 CCDs (4 L3 instances, 3 active cores each) — IF-capped at ~125-160 GB/s while the memory subsystem is FULLY populated (author confirms 8 channels, 128 GB) and can do ~190+. The 3975WX (32c, 8 CCDs) moves the bottleneck to the memory ceiling: +20-50% effective bandwidth AND ~2.7x aggregate AVX2 SIMD for Strata's expert pool — the two exact axes the pool needs, at <500 EUR, the best $/tok/s hardware buy on the list (ahead of the 5060 Ti). Purchase check: seller pulls from P620s. Install at the SAME maintenance window as the 5060 Ti (end of the cycle-2 pass, night of Oct 6-7 or Oct 7-8): one HW-v1/HW-v2 boundary, gpu_inventory (extended to CPU at that point) + engine build recorded per run; then the --gpu-only-full bench on the new machine before any platform-jump decision.
