--- body ---
## Context

Padme's local model seat is qwen3.8-27b on llama.cpp (:8080). Strata — the
single-purpose engine for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next — was installed this session with
the Coder variant (IQ1_M) on :8081. The tournament decides which stack serves
padme's local seats for harness work, against the hosted workhorses (Opus,
Sol, GLM 5.3) as value anchors. It measures stacks (model x engine bundled),
not either factor alone; the verdict drives routing (AGENTS.md
external-reviewer routing, models.json).

Concept note (rule book): docs/2026-10-03-model-tournament-concept.md

The instrument is candidate-agnostic (concept note §8): this ticket's cycle
is six arms — local 27B, Coder, 35B-A3B, hosted Opus, Sol, GLM 5.3 — and
candidates are declared in the tournament config, so future cycles may enter
the Qwen 4 family or other hosted tiers (Terra/Sonnet) under the same rules,
with cost as a first-class outcome, the egress boundary for hosted arms, and
judges disjoint from the candidate set.

TRACKING TICKET — stays open until all phases land and the routing verdict is
recorded. Children are opened at hunt time with cross-references here.

## Protocol summary (full text in the concept note)

- Full crossover: all six arms attempt every sampled ticket (k=6: 27B on
  :8080, Coder on :8081, 35B-A3B on :8082, Opus hosted, Sol hosted, GLM 5.3
  hosted), fresh historical worktree per run at the ticket's original base
  commit. Local arms serialize on padme's GPUs; hosted arms run on provider
  hardware at their recommended default effort.
- Sample: closed tickets; pre-registered strata (project x type x difficulty,
  deliberately including non-coding work); random draw within strata;
  N = 10 drawn (60 runs at k=6), seed 20261003, artifacts ~/arena/inventory.json
  and ~/arena/sample.json; author approval pending.
- Validity: provider assertion per run (0979 rule; mismatch voids the run),
  strict serialization (local arms never resident together), randomised
  within-ticket order, time-filtered memory (no post-ticket content), t0 =
  /health OK, matched knobs for local arms (reasoning effort, sampling,
  retry budgets, concurrency cap), tool-calling smoke test before the
  tournament (done, all six arms PASS).
- Judging: SPEED = wall-clock on an unloaded padme (runner asserts idle GPUs
  + low load; date and hour recorded per run); COST = money (provider balance
  before/after each hosted run where a balance API exists, else tokens x
  pre-registered prices; tokens recorded always); CORRECTNESS = boxing
  scoring from 10 points, fixed deductions REROLL -3 / CHANGES -2 /
  COMMENTS -1 / NITS -0.5, floor 0, DNF 0 — common vocabulary in
  ~/arena/judge-rubric.md (panel disjoint from candidate families; fresh
  judge sessions; normalized submission packages are the only channel).
- Recording: full conversation transcripts archived per run (passes and
  hiccups alike); post-tournament transcript analysis is harness-tuning
  material. Arm B's 65K context sufficiency is a studied question answered
  with data.

## Children (to be opened at hunt time)

- sample selection and worktrees: strata pre-registration done (this
  session); pending author approval, then historical worktrees at merge^ and
  time-filtered memory per ticket

Session-close children (created 2026-10-06, the "what's next" slate):

- 1046 PDF report (graphs, Pareto, clusters, situation guide) — satisfies
  the parent's "paired analysis written up" exit criterion
- 1047 blog posts (Blocked-by 1046)
- 1048 cycle 3: locals @medium vs hosted flash lineage twin (DashScope
  direct), --expert-profile-save on the Strata arms, engine duel if a
  viable llama.cpp GGUF exists
- 1049 HW-v2 merged install window (5060 Ti + 3975WX), rebuild 86;120,
  prefill #448 before/after
